  "correct": "1",
  "solution": "The logic followed here is:\n\nLogic: **Second number = First number × (Third number)²**\n\n**(9, 576, 8)**\n\n→ 576 = 9 × (8)2\n\n→ 576 = 9 × 64\n\n**(7, 252, 6) **\n\n→ 252 = 7 × (6)2\n\n→ 252 = 7 × 36\n\nNow, let's check each option,\n\n1) **(10, 40, 2)**\n\n→ 40 = 10 × (2)2\n\n→ 40 = 10 × 4 ⇒ **Follows the logic.**\n\n2) **(4, 82, 5) **\n\n→ 82 = 4 × (5)2\n\n→ 82 ≠ 4 × 25 \n\n3) **(15, 210, 7)**\n\n→ 210 = 15 × (7)2\n\n→ 210 ≠ 15 × 49\n\n4) **(8, 650, 10)**\n\n→ 650 = 8 × (10)2\n\n→ 650 ≠ 8 × 100 \n\nHere, we can see that only Option 1 follows the logic.\n\nHence, the correct answer is **\"****(10, 40, 2)\"**.",
